.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/normalize-path Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "normalize-path [![NPM version](https://img.shields.io/npm/v/normalize-path.svg?style=flat)](https://www.npmjs.com/package/normalize-path) [![NPM monthly downloads](https://img.shields.io/npm/dm/normalize-path.svg?style=flat)](https://npmjs.org/package/normalize-path) [![NPM total downloads](https://img.shields.io/npm/dt/normalize-path.svg?style=flat)](https://npmjs.org/package/normalize-path) [![Linux Build Status](https://img.shields.io/travis/jonschlinkert/normalize-path.svg?style=flat&label=Travis)](https://travis-ci.org/jonschlinkert/normalize-path)"
.PP
.RS 4
Normalize slashes in a file path to be posix/unix-like forward slashes\&. Also condenses repeat slashes to a single slash and removes and trailing slashes, unless disabled\&. 
.RE
.PP

.PP
Please consider following this project's author, \fRJon Schlinkert\fP, and consider starring the project to show your :heart: and support\&.
.SH "Install"
.PP
Install with \fRnpm\fP:

.PP
.PP
.nf
$ npm install \-\-save normalize\-path
.fi
.PP
.SH "Usage"
.PP
.PP
.nf
const normalize = require('normalize\-path');

console\&.log(normalize('\\\\foo\\\\bar\\\\baz\\\\')); 
//=> '/foo/bar/baz'
.fi
.PP

.PP
\fBwin32 namespaces\fP

.PP
.PP
.nf
console\&.log(normalize('\\\\\\\\?\\\\UNC\\\\Server01\\\\user\\\\docs\\\\Letter\&.txt')); 
//=> '//?/UNC/Server01/user/docs/Letter\&.txt'

console\&.log(normalize('\\\\\\\\\&.\\\\CdRomX')); 
//=> '//\&./CdRomX'
.fi
.PP

.PP
\fBConsecutive slashes\fP

.PP
Condenses multiple consecutive forward slashes (except for leading slashes in win32 namespaces) to a single slash\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
console\&.log(normalize('\&.//foo//bar///////baz/')); 
//=> '\&./foo/bar/baz'
.fi
.PP
.SS "Trailing slashes"
By default trailing slashes are removed\&. Pass \fRfalse\fP as the last argument to disable this behavior and \fI\fBkeep\fP trailing slashes\fP:

.PP
.PP
.nf
console\&.log(normalize('foo\\\\bar\\\\baz\\\\', false)); //=> 'foo/bar/baz/'
console\&.log(normalize('\&./foo/bar/baz/', false)); //=> '\&./foo/bar/baz/'
.fi
.PP
.SH "Release history"
.PP
.SS "v3\&.0"
No breaking changes in this release\&.

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
a check was added to ensure that \fRwin32 namespaces\fP are handled properly by win32 \fRpath\&.parse()\fP after a path has been normalized by this library\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
a minor optimization was made to simplify how the trailing separator was handled
.PP
